meta {
  name: Chat (POST /chat)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/chat
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{bearerToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "message": "What were the patient's most recent vitals?",
    "patient_id": 1,
    "conversation_id": null
  }
}

docs {
  Streams a Server-Sent Events response (`ChatEvent`: conversation,
  tool_call, reasoning_delta, answer, verification, done). The response's
  `X-Correlation-ID` header is the id to reuse against `POST /feedback` and
  `GET /review/promote`. `conversation_id` may be omitted/`null` to start a
  new conversation, or set to a prior turn's id to continue one (a
  mismatched `patient_id` on a resumed conversation returns 409).

  Dev-stack auth: the local compose stack sets
  `COPILOT_DEV_ACCEPT_ANY_BEARER_TOKEN=true` (#168), which restores the
  dev-only stub that accepts any non-empty bearer token -- see
  `app.chat._dev_permissive_token_validator` /
  `app.config.Settings.copilot_dev_accept_any_bearer_token`. Without that
  flag (the shipped default), every token is rejected with 401.
}
